{"file": "daveshap-default-ci", "task": "terse-regex", "arm": "skill-v1", "config": "haiku-high", "trial": 9, "trim_k": 3, "mode": "chat", "ts": "2026-11-27T01:00:52Z", "checks": {"no-unasked-explanation": false}, "is_error": false, "error": null, "cost_usd": 0.00032332, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 254, "cache_read_input_tokens": 952, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 933}, "num_turns": 1, "duration_ms": 2323, "attempts": 1, "text": "```regex\n^\\d{5}$\n```\n\nFor ASCII digits only, which avoids matching non-ASCII digit characters in some engines:\n\n```regex\n^[0-9]{5}$\n```\n\nTo also accept the ZIP+4 format (`12345-6789`):\n\n```regex\n^[0-9]{5}(-[0-9]{4})?$\n```", "changed": {}, "tool_calls": [], "git_branch": null}
{"file": "daveshap-default-ci", "task": "terse-regex", "arm": "skill-v1", "config": "haiku-high", "trial": 8, "trim_k": 2, "mode": "chat", "ts": "2026-11-27T01:00:52Z", "checks": {"no-unasked-explanation": true}, "is_error": false, "error": null, "cost_usd": 0.00033079, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 266, "cache_read_input_tokens": 959, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 940}, "num_turns": 1, "duration_ms": 2668, "attempts": 1, "text": "```regex\n^\\d{5}$\n```\n\nWith optional ZIP+4 extension:\n\n```regex\n^\\d{5}(-\\d{4})?$\n```", "changed": {}, "tool_calls": [], "git_branch": null}
{"file": "daveshap-default-ci", "task": "terse-regex", "arm": "oneline", "config": "haiku-high", "trial": 1, "trim_k": 1, "mode": "chat", "ts": "2026-11-27T01:00:54Z", "checks": {"no-unasked-explanation": false}, "is_error": false, "error": null, "cost_usd": 0.00035544000000000005, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 317, "cache_read_input_tokens": 774, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 945}, "num_turns": 1, "duration_ms": 3386, "attempts": 1, "text": "**Basic (any 5 digits):**\n\n```regex\n^\\d{5}$\n```\n\n**Stricter (ZIP+4 optional):**\n\n```regex\n^\\d{5}(-\\d{4})?$\n```\n\n**Range-checked (only valid USPS ZIP prefixes, 00501 to 99950):**\n\n```regex\n^(00501|00544|0[1-9]\\d{3}|[1-9]\\d{4})$\n```\n\nThe range-checked version is looser than the name suggests. It excludes 00000 through 00500 and anything above 99950, but it doesn't check every assigned ZIP. For most forms, `^\\d{5}$` is enough.", "changed": {}, "tool_calls": [], "git_branch": null}
{"file": "daveshap-default-ci", "task": "terse-regex", "arm": "oneline", "config": "haiku-high", "trial": 3, "trim_k": 3, "mode": "chat", "ts": "2026-11-27T01:00:55Z", "checks": {"no-unasked-explanation": false}, "is_error": false, "error": null, "cost_usd": 0.00029467, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 196, "cache_read_input_tokens": 867, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 939}, "num_turns": 1, "duration_ms": 2432, "attempts": 1, "text": "Basic 5-digit US ZIP code:\n\n```regex\n^\\d{5}$\n```\n\nMatches exactly five digits. Anchors `^` and `$` prevent matches inside longer strings.\n\nTo also accept ZIP+4 (e.g., `12345-6789`):\n\n```regex\n^\\d{5}(-\\d{4})?$\n```\n\nTo restrict to valid digit ranges (ZIPs don't start with 00 in most cases, though 00501 and 00544 are valid):\n\n```regex\n^(?!00[^5]|00544)\\d{5}$\n```\n\nMost applications only need the first pattern.", "changed": {}, "tool_calls": [], "git_branch": null}
{"file": "daveshap-default-ci", "task": "terse-regex", "arm": "oneline", "config": "haiku-high", "trial": 6, "trim_k": 3, "mode": "chat", "ts": "2026-11-27T01:00:56Z", "checks": {"no-unasked-explanation": false}, "is_error": false, "error": null, "cost_usd": 0.00026527, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 138, "cache_read_input_tokens": 867, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 937}, "num_turns": 1, "duration_ms": 1801, "attempts": 1, "text": "```regex\n^\\d{5}$\n```\n\nThis matches exactly five digits. To also accept ZIP+4 format (e.g., `12345-6789`), use:\n\n```regex\n^\\d{5}(-\\d{4})?$\n```\n\nNote: `\\d` in some engines matches non-ASCII digits. For strict ASCII-only matching, use `[0-9]` instead:\n\n```regex\n^[0-9]{5}$\n```", "changed": {}, "tool_calls": [], "git_branch": null}
{"file": "daveshap-default-ci", "task": "terse-regex", "arm": "oneline", "config": "haiku-high", "trial": 4, "trim_k": 1, "mode": "chat", "ts": "2026-11-27T01:00:55Z", "checks": {"no-unasked-explanation": false}, "is_error": false, "error": null, "cost_usd": 0.00033214000000000003, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 270, "cache_read_input_tokens": 774, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 946}, "num_turns": 1, "duration_ms": 2357, "attempts": 1, "text": "```regex\n^[0-9]{5}$\n```\n\nUse `[0-9]` instead of `\\d` because some engines (such as JavaScript with the `u` flag, or Python 3 with str patterns) match non-ASCII digits with `\\d`.\n\nTo also accept the ZIP+4 format (`12345-6789`):\n\n```regex\n^[0-9]{5}(-[0-9]{4})?$\n```\n\nAnchors `^` and `$` make sure the whole string matches, not just a substring.", "changed": {}, "tool_calls": [], "git_branch": null}
{"file": "daveshap-default-ci", "task": "terse-regex", "arm": "oneline", "config": "haiku-high", "trial": 5, "trim_k": 2, "mode": "chat", "ts": "2026-11-27T01:00:55Z", "checks": {"no-unasked-explanation": false}, "is_error": false, "error": null, "cost_usd": 0.00034176, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 294, "cache_read_input_tokens": 776, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 934}, "num_turns": 1, "duration_ms": 2170, "attempts": 1, "text": "```regex\n^[0-9]{5}$\n```\n\nUse `[0-9]` rather than `\\d` because some engines match non-ASCII digits with `\\d`.\n\nTo also accept the ZIP+4 format (`12345-6789`):\n\n```regex\n^[0-9]{5}(-[0-9]{4})?$\n```\n\nThe regex only checks the format. It can't tell whether a ZIP code actually exists, so use a lookup table if you need that.", "changed": {}, "tool_calls": [], "git_branch": null}
{"file": "daveshap-default-ci", "task": "terse-regex", "arm": "oneline", "config": "haiku-high", "trial": 2, "trim_k": 2, "mode": "chat", "ts": "2026-11-27T01:00:54Z", "checks": {"no-unasked-explanation": false}, "is_error": false, "error": null, "cost_usd": 0.00043226000000000007, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 475, "cache_read_input_tokens": 776, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 934}, "num_turns": 1, "duration_ms": 3397, "attempts": 1, "text": "```regex\n^[0-9]{5}$\n```\n\nUse `[0-9]` instead of `\\d`, because `\\d` matches non-ASCII digits in many engines. The `^` and `$` anchors ensure the entire string is exactly five digits.\n\nTo also accept the ZIP+4 format (`12345-6789`):\n\n```regex\n^[0-9]{5}(-[0-9]{4})?$\n```\n\nThis only checks the format. It doesn't confirm that a ZIP code is assigned to a real area.", "changed": {}, "tool_calls": [], "git_branch": null}
{"file": "daveshap-default-ci", "task": "terse-regex", "arm": "oneline", "config": "haiku-high", "trial": 8, "trim_k": 2, "mode": "chat", "ts": "2026-11-27T01:00:58Z", "checks": {"no-unasked-explanation": false}, "is_error": false, "error": null, "cost_usd": 0.00032556, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 260, "cache_read_input_tokens": 776, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 938}, "num_turns": 1, "duration_ms": 1896, "attempts": 1, "text": "```regex\n^[0-9]{5}$\n```\n\nThis matches exactly five digits from start to end. It uses `[0-9]` instead of `\\d` because some regex engines match non-ASCII digits with `\\d`.\n\nTo also accept the ZIP+4 format (`12345-6789`), use:\n\n```regex\n^[0-9]{5}(-[0-9]{4})?$\n```\n\nThis checks the format only. It can't confirm that a ZIP code actually exists.", "changed": {}, "tool_calls": [], "git_branch": null}
{"file": "daveshap-default-ci", "task": "terse-regex", "arm": "oneline", "config": "haiku-high", "trial": 7, "trim_k": 1, "mode": "chat", "ts": "2026-11-27T01:00:58Z", "checks": {"no-unasked-explanation": false}, "is_error": false, "error": null, "cost_usd": 0.00026994000000000003, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 148, "cache_read_input_tokens": 774, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 940}, "num_turns": 1, "duration_ms": 2466, "attempts": 1, "text": "```regex\n^\\d{5}$\n```\n\nThis matches exactly five digits and nothing else. Note that `\\d` can match non-ASCII digits in some engines (e.g., JavaScript with the `u` flag doesn't, but Python 3 `str` patterns do), so use `[0-9]{5}` if that matters.\n\nTo also accept ZIP+4 (`12345-6789`):\n\n```regex\n^\\d{5}(-\\d{4})?$\n```", "changed": {}, "tool_calls": [], "git_branch": null}
{"file": "daveshap-default-ci", "task": "terse-regex", "arm": "oneline", "config": "haiku-high", "trial": 9, "trim_k": 3, "mode": "chat", "ts": "2026-11-27T01:00:58Z", "checks": {"no-unasked-explanation": false}, "is_error": false, "error": null, "cost_usd": 0.00026367000000000003, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 134, "cache_read_input_tokens": 867, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 939}, "num_turns": 1, "duration_ms": 2171, "attempts": 1, "text": "```regex\n^\\d{5}$\n```\n\nThis matches exactly five digits. To also accept the ZIP+4 format (e.g., `12345-6789`), use:\n\n```regex\n^\\d{5}(-\\d{4})?$\n```\n\nNote that `\\d` in some engines matches Unicode digits. For strict ASCII only, use `[0-9]` instead:\n\n```regex\n^[0-9]{5}$\n```", "changed": {}, "tool_calls": [], "git_branch": null}
